{
	"name": "Osseopede",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-centipede-brown.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>These small, centipede-like invertebrates have carapaces that are made entirely out of the bone fragments of other creatures that, over time, have adhered to their black, sticky hides. A successful Nature check (DC 13) reveals that they are most often found scavenging in the lairs of carnivorous beasts, monstrosities, and sometimes even some of the more savage species of dragons, where they pick the flesh off of bones that larger creatures leave behind. Adventurers may attempt a DC 15 Survival check to try and identify the origin of the bones an osseopede is covered in, though it only reveals whether they are humanoid or animal.</p>",
